      "content": "The person who was \"on the screen\" was a performance, and it's natural to feel lost when the script ends. What you're feeling is the deep ache of a life that feels unmoored, and that feeling of pointlessness is a very real indicator of how much you're hurting. Instead of trying to rebuild the old version, perhaps you could focus on finding a quiet, small way to *feel* something again, even if it's just a tiny flicker of something new.",
