      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The weight you feel is the weight of a life that was built on a fragile, outdated idea of yourself. Accepting that the story is over is the final, most absolute form of surrender, and it sounds incredibly tempting right now. It's not about pretending; it's about letting go of the impossible standard you set for yourself. A gentle, quiet act of self-caring—like just letting yourself rest—is a valid way to start honoring the shell, even if it feels empty.",
